@tradition rec-regatta
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// The river regatta: every 4 weeks on a Sunday from Day 21 (21, 49, 77...), 09:30-11:00, the river hall; heats of four round
// the loop (on paper), Holt's horn, the winner's pennant over the dock; you paddle the fun heat. Watchers on the banks and
// the concourse glass (RA's river-banks venue). A gathering.
k: 490
title: River regatta
when: every 4 weeks sunday week 3
at: 09:30-11:00
min: 30
prio: 1
jitter: 20
where: 7 room River hall: rec:kayak
hold: none
who: holt always, watch 45%, juniors 35%, everyone 25%
anim: everyone talk
host: holt
from: holt
flag: rec.on

== mail
- The river regatta is tomorrow, {time} in the river hall. Heats of four round the loop, Chief Holt on the horn, and the winner's pennant over the dock. Watch from the bank, or paddle the fun heat.

== ask
- Regatta morning! I'm in heat two. Wish me luck. Wish my arms luck.   #funny
- Coming to the regatta? Cheer from the bank, or paddle the fun heat. No times in that one.
- Holt's got the horn out. That means it's serious.   #funny

== here
- Go, go, go! Round the bend!
- Here's the horn. Everyone hold on.
- Fun heat next. Anyone can go. Even you.   #funny

== thanks
- You find a spot on the bank as Chief Holt raises the horn. Four kayaks wait in the slow channel.

== chatter
- Who got the pennant? It's up over the dock now.
- The officers could hear the regatta horn through the floor. Twice.   #funny
- I came last in my heat. With style, though.   #funny
